commit 5c41539b01ae695e2191d66eb996e63efb7099a9
Author: Sauyon Lee <git@sjle.co>
Date:   Sat Oct 24 08:59:33 2026 +0000

    orca: unmappable Hyprland binds no longer fail the build

    Review round 6: the generator threw on any bind it could not translate, so
    an ordinary bare Print screenshot bind, or SUPER + grave, would have broken
    every desktop host's build over a Hyprland edit. Only an unknown modifier
    fails now -- it may be a real Orca chord. A key Orca has no name for cannot
    collide with one and is skipped with a log line; bare keys are checked with
    Orca's bare-chord rules; Hyprland's aliases (MOD4/WIN/LOGO, MOD1, grave,
    Prior/Next) map.

    Also: the merge's withdrawal-restore path is gone, dead since ownership went
    per key; the build's smoke merge now asserts the table and the seed landed;
    tests pin a UI reset re-applying and common/linux layering.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: acde1bb17f31

